@node Introduction
@unnumbered Introduction

@acronym{STARTER} (@emph{Simple distribuTed smART conTrollER}) is a
distributed automation core. @command{starter-configurable-service}
(@acronym{STCS}) bridges the outside world to starter-core inputs and
outputs using an @acronym{XML} pipeline.

@command{starter-configurable-adapter} (@acronym{STCA}) is a smaller,
independent process that sits @emph{in front of} @acronym{STCS}. It loads
exactly one plugin that talks to a complex external source (cloud
@acronym{API}, fieldbus, @dots{}), keeps a numeric snapshot in memory, and
exposes that snapshot over a common @acronym{HTTP}/@acronym{JSON} API.
@acronym{STCS} can then use its existing @code{http-transport} and
@code{json-reader} / writers against that API---without embedding the
source protocol inside the service.

This manual is organised in two layers:

@itemize
@item
@emph{Presentation} chapters explain what the adapter is, how data moves,
and how to build and run it.
@item
The @ref{Configuration Reference} and @ref{HTTP Reference} spell out
options and endpoints. @ref{Writing Plugins} explains how to add a new
source plugin (in-tree or as a separate repository).
@end itemize

