@node Role Versus STCS
@section Role Versus STCS

Typical end-to-end flows:

@example
external source
  → STCA plugin
  → data-ready → adapter store
  → GET /data (HTTP JSON)
  → STCS http-transport + json-reader
  → starter STInput
@end example

@example
starter STOutput
  → STCS writer + http-transport
  → PUT/POST /data (HTTP JSON)
  → STCA write_value(s)
  → external source
@end example

Unlike @acronym{STCS}, @acronym{STCA} does @emph{not} own datapoints,
transports, or starter-core bindings. It owns one plugin instance and one
in-memory value store, and speaks a fixed numeric @acronym{HTTP} dialect.

@node One Plugin Per Process
@section One Plugin Per Process

Each adapter process loads plugins from a directory, but the
configuration must name @emph{exactly one} @code{<plugin>}. That plugin
collects from the source on its own schedule (timers, threads, @dots{})
and pushes updates into the adapter. To run two sources, run two adapter
instances (different ports / configs).

Product plugins are usually separate repositories (one plugin per repo)
and install into the same plugin directory as the in-tree @code{dummy}
example.

@node Values and Access Flags
@section Values and Access Flags

All live values are @code{gdouble}, keyed by a string. Each stored entry
is an @code{STCAValue}:

@itemize
@item
@code{value} --- the number
@item
@code{access} --- bitmask of @code{STCA_ACCESS_READ} and/or
@code{STCA_ACCESS_WRITE}, serialized on the wire as @code{r}, @code{w},
or @code{rw}
@end itemize

The @acronym{HTTP} layer rejects writes to keys that are not writable
(@code{403}) @emph{before} calling the plugin. Unknown keys return
@code{404}.

@node Data Ready Signal
@section The @code{data-ready} Signal

The adapter is the owner of the value store. Plugins do not keep a
long-lived table for @acronym{HTTP}; they build a batch
(@code{GHashTable} of @code{gchar*} → @code{STCAValue*}), emit
@code{data-ready}, and the adapter merges a deep copy into
@code{context->values}.

Emit once per collection cycle (multi-key batch), not once per key.

@node Write Path
@section Write Path

@code{PUT}/@code{POST} handlers call @code{stca_plugin_write_value} or
@code{stca_plugin_write_values} synchronously. On success the adapter
updates the stored numbers for those keys so a subsequent @code{GET}
reflects the command. The plugin may later emit @code{data-ready} with
authoritative values read back from the source.

@node Building and Installing
@chapter Building and Installing

@menu
* Dependencies::
