@end menu

@node Command Line
@section Command Line

@example
starter-configurable-adapter [OPTION...]
@end example

@table @option
@item -h, --help
Print a short usage summary and exit.

@item -c, --config=@var{FILE}
Path to the adapter configuration file (required).

@item -P, --config-preprocessor=@var{CMD}
Shell command used to preprocess the config before parsing.
@code{@{F@}} is replaced with the config path. An empty value disables
preprocessing. Default may also come from
@env{STCA_CONFIG_PREPROCESSOR}.

@item -p, --plugin-dir=@var{DIR}
Directory to scan for @code{.so} plugins. Falls back to
@env{STCA_PLUGIN_PATH}, then the compile-time default install path.

@item -V, --version
Print the version string and exit.
@end table

Startup order: scan plugins → parse @acronym{XML} → start @acronym{HTTP}
server → @code{stca_plugin_start} → @code{g_main_loop_run}.

@node Logging
@section Logging

The adapter uses GLib message logging. Domains follow component names
(@code{main}, @code{config}, @code{http}, @code{plugin}, and the
plugin's own domain). Use the usual GLib environment variables
(@env{G_MESSAGES_DEBUG}, @dots{}) when debugging.

From the build tree (example with @code{dummy}):

@example
$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=lib/.libs \
    src/starter-configurable-adapter \
      -c examples/dummy/dummy.stca.xml \
      -p plugins/dummy/.libs
@end example

@node Configuration Overview
@chapter Configuration Overview

Root element @samp{stca} with a @code{version} attribute, one
@samp{global} block, and exactly one @samp{plugin}:

@example
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<stca version="1">
  <global>
    <listen-address>127.0.0.1</listen-address>
    <listen-port>8080</listen-port>
    <adapter-name>STCA:Dummy</adapter-name>
  </global>
  <plugin name="dummy">
    <!-- opaque subtree for the plugin -->
  </plugin>
</stca>
@end example

The @code{name} attribute must match @code{stca_plugin_info_get_name()}
of a scanned module. Child elements of @samp{plugin} are passed unchanged
to @code{stca_plugin_configure()}.

@node Configuration Reference
@chapter Configuration Reference

@menu
* Document and Global Reference::
* Plugin Element Reference::
* Out-of-tree Plugins::
@end menu

@node Document and Global Reference
@section Document and Global

@table @code
@item stca/@@version
Document format version. Use @code{1}.

@item global/listen-address
Address for the @acronym{HTTP} server (default none / all interfaces
depending on libsoup listen behaviour; examples use @code{127.0.0.1}).

@item global/listen-port
@acronym{TCP} port (default @code{8080}).

@item global/adapter-name
Human-readable name returned by @code{GET /info}
(default @code{STCA}).
@end table

@node Plugin Element Reference
@section Plugin Element

@table @code
@item plugin/@@name
Required. Must match a loaded plugin module name.

@item plugin/*
Opaque to the adapter. Interpreted only by the plugin's
@code{configure} implementation.
@end table

@node Out-of-tree Plugins
@section Out-of-tree Plugins

This package ships only the @code{dummy} example. Product plugins are
separate repositories---one plugin per repo---and install into the same
plugin directory. Build them against an installed adapter:

@example
$ pkg-config --cflags --libs starter-configurable-adapter
@end example

or against a local build tree:

@example
$ ./configure --with-stca=/path/to/configurable-adapter
@end example

@node HTTP Reference
@chapter HTTP Reference

All successful @acronym{JSON} bodies use @code{Content-Type:
application/json}. Numbers on the write path are plain @acronym{JSON}
numbers (or a @acronym{JSON} object of numbers for bulk write).

@menu
* Health and Info::
* Reading Data::
* Writing Data::
@end menu

@node Health and Info
@section Health and Info

@table @code
@item GET /health
@example
@{"status":"ok"@}
@end example

@item GET /info
@example
@{
  "adapter-name": "STCA:Dummy",
  "adapter-version": "1.0.0",
  "plugin": "dummy",
  "plugin-version": "1.0.0"
@}
@end example
@end table

@node Reading Data
@section Reading Data

@table @code
@item GET /data
@acronym{JSON} object keyed by datapoint name. Each value is an object:

@example
@{
  "temperature": @{ "value": 21.5, "access": "r" @},
  "setpoint":    @{ "value": 22.0, "access": "rw" @}
@}
@end example

@item GET /data/@var{key}
Single entry in the same @code{@{ "value", "access" @}} shape, or
@code{404} if the key is unknown.
@end table

@node Writing Data
@section Writing Data

@table @code
@item PUT /data/@var{key}
@itemx POST /data/@var{key}
Body: a @acronym{JSON} number. On success: @code{204 No Content}.

@item PUT /data
@itemx POST /data
Body: a @acronym{JSON} object of string keys to numbers. On success:
@code{204 No Content}.
@end table

Errors:

@table @code
@item 403
Key exists but is not writable, or the plugin rejected the write with a
permission error.

@item 404
Unknown key (or missing key in the path).

@item 400
Malformed @acronym{JSON} body.
@end table

The adapter checks the stored @code{access} flags before invoking the
plugin.

@node Writing Plugins
@chapter Writing Plugins

@menu
