@node Plugin Exports
@section Required Exports

Each module must export:

@example
STCAPluginInfo *stca_plugin_get_info (void);
GObject        *stca_plugin_create (void);
@end example

@code{stca_plugin_get_info} returns a new @code{STCAPluginInfo} with a
stable @code{name} (used in @acronym{XML}) and @code{version}.
@code{stca_plugin_create} returns a new instance of your
@code{STCAPlugin} subclass.

@node Plugin Lifecycle
@section Lifecycle

@enumerate
@item
The adapter scans @code{*.so} files and records info by name.
@item
Configuration selects one name and calls @code{stca_plugin_create}, then
@code{stca_plugin_configure(plugin, <plugin> node)}.
@item
After the @acronym{HTTP} server is listening, the adapter calls
@code{stca_plugin_start}.
@item
On shutdown it calls @code{stca_plugin_stop}.
@end enumerate

Implement the virtual methods on @code{STCAPluginClass}:
@code{configure}, @code{start}, @code{stop}, @code{write_value}, and
optionally @code{write_values}.

@node Emitting Values
@section Emitting Values

@example
GHashTable *batch = g_hash_table_new_full (g_str_hash, g_str_equal,
                                           g_free,
                                           (GDestroyNotify) stca_value_free);
g_hash_table_insert (batch, g_strdup ("temperature"),
                     stca_value_new (21.5, STCA_ACCESS_READ));
g_hash_table_insert (batch, g_strdup ("setpoint"),
                     stca_value_new (22.0,
                                    STCA_ACCESS_READ | STCA_ACCESS_WRITE));
stca_plugin_emit_data_ready (STCA_PLUGIN (self), batch);
g_hash_table_unref (batch);
@end example

The signal payload is transfer-none for the duration of handlers; the
adapter copies what it needs.

@node Handling Writes
@section Handling Writes

@code{write_value} receives @code{(plugin, key, value, error)} and must
apply the change to the external source synchronously, returning
@code{FALSE} and setting @code{GError} on failure. Prefer implementing
@code{write_value}; the default @code{write_values} loops over keys.

@node Building a Plugin
@section Building and Installing

Link against @code{libstarter-configurable-adapter} and install the
module with @code{-module -avoid-version} into the adapter plugin
directory. Public headers live under
@file{starter/configurable-adapter/} (@file{plugin.h}, @file{log.h}).

Out-of-tree projects typically use Autotools with
@code{PKG_CHECK_MODULES([STCA], [starter-configurable-adapter])} or
@option{--with-stca=DIR} pointing at an uninstalled build tree.

@node Examples Directory
@chapter Examples Directory

@menu
* Dummy Example::
@end menu

@node Dummy Example
@section Dummy (@file{examples/dummy/dummy.stca.xml})

The @code{dummy} plugin is a timer-driven mock used to exercise the
@acronym{HTTP} API. It emits @code{temperature}, @code{humidity}, and
@code{online} as read-only, and @code{setpoint} as read-write. The
plugin option @code{interval-ms} sets the emit period (default
@code{5000}).

@example
$ curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/data
$ curl -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8080/data/setpoint \
    -d '22.5' -H 'Content-Type: application/json'
# temperature is read-only → 403
@end example

